  "worked_solution": "We shall use the following identity:\n\n$$\n\u2207\\times (f\\,F)=f\u2207\\times F+\u2207f\\times F\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute $\u2207f\\times F.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u2207f\\times F & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -2x & 1 & 0 \\\\ x & 0 & yz\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =[1(yz)-0(0)]i-[-2x(yz)-0(x)]j+[-2x(0)-1(x)]k \\\\  & =yz\\,i+2xyz\\,j-x\\,k \\\\  & =\u27e8yz,2xyz,-x\u27e9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u2207\\times (f\\,F) & =f\u2207\\times F+\u2207f\\times F \\\\  & =(y-{x}^{2})\u27e8z,0,0\u27e9+\u27e8yz,2xyz,-x\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e8z(y-{x}^{2}),0,0\u27e9+\u27e8yz,2xyz,-x\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e8z(2y-{x}^{2}),2xyz,-x\u27e9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u2207\\times (f\\,F)(0,2,-1) & =\u27e8(-1)(2(2)-(0)^{2}),2(0)(2)(-1),-0\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e8-4,0,0\u27e9.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
